From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] viogpu_umd: swap chain buffers DWM composes without a copy

A present copied the buffer to a readback buffer on the GPU, waited, copied it on the CPU into the kernel
allocation, and the kernel driver uploaded it again for every composition: at 2560x1440 5.3 ms a present (184 fps
for a clear and present; 1080p 290, 720p 526; D3D11 ~0.4 ms).

Swap chain buffers (committed on a primary heap) in RGBA8, BGRA8, RGB10A2 or RGBA16F, one level, layer and sample,
no UAVs, are now shared: their kernel allocation asks the host for a texture made from Vulkan memory
(VIOGPU_UMD_VIRGL_BIND_VK_SHARED, virglrenderer image patch 0012; no GDI-surface uploads), its host resource id
(VIOGPU_RES_INFO) names that memory to Venus (VkImportMemoryResourceInfoMESA; Venus' renderer has the kernel driver
attach it, kvm-guest-drivers-windows 0022, mesa-venus 0007), and the buffer is a Venus image of the host's
parameters on it, wrapped by vkd3d-proton (CreateResourceFromBorrowedHandle; the driver frees image and memory).
Present waits for the queue as before and copies nothing: 0.3 ms at every size (~2300-3000 fps). GL keeps BGRA as
RGBA, so a BGRA buffer stays vkd3d-proton's own and Present blits it into its shared RGBA image (the blit swaps the
channels; recorded through vkd3d-proton's Vulkan interop on the present queue): 0.7 ms (1100-1400 fps). Anything
missing (format, flags, host or driver support, an import the host refuses) leaves nothing behind and makes a copied
buffer as before. The runtime refused a swap chain allocation of size 0, so the shared one keeps its (unused) guest
pages.
---
diff --git a/libs/viogpu_umd/umd_bridge.c b/libs/viogpu_umd/umd_bridge.c
index 486aa6d4..f3e58e4c 100644
--- a/libs/viogpu_umd/umd_bridge.c
+++ b/libs/viogpu_umd/umd_bridge.c
@@ -93,6 +93,21 @@ static ID3D12DXVKInteropDevice1 *bridge_interop(void *device)
     return interop;
 }
 
+long viogpu_bridge_create_borrowed_resource(void *device, const void *desc, unsigned long long vk_image,
+        void **resource)
+{
+    ID3D12DeviceExt1 *ext = NULL;
+    ID3D12Device *d = device;
+    HRESULT hr;
+
+    *resource = NULL;
+    if (FAILED(hr = d->lpVtbl->QueryInterface(d, &IID_ID3D12DeviceExt1, (void **)&ext)))
+        return hr;
+    hr = ext->lpVtbl->CreateResourceFromBorrowedHandle(ext, desc, vk_image, (ID3D12Resource **)resource);
+    ext->lpVtbl->Release(ext);
+    return hr;
+}
+
 long viogpu_bridge_vk_handles(void *device, void **instance, void **physical_device, void **vk_device)
 {
     ID3D12DXVKInteropDevice1 *interop = bridge_interop(device);
